  "notes": "\"The single most extreme sub in the Bay canon\" — near-static, extremely long note values, tuned for car resonance — so this model has the lowest bass in the batch (register floor 21), the highest `followRootsProb` at 0.95, `glideProb` 0.05 and no passing tones at all, and its groove is \"deliberately dragging\": the slowest kick, `quantizeStrength` 0.79, hats that stop. ⚠ The bass is `mirror_kick` rather than a held note for the reason this whole dataset avoids `reese_sustain` — one note per chord saturates — and over a kick that plays 1 and 3 that reads as sustained at 90 BPM. The harmony is the other documented fact and it is unusual for the lane: the source was **replayed**, not sampled, because the producer found the record too fast pitched down and re-performed it \"to control the breaks\", so what is authored is a short minor cycle with an R&B-style ii–V rather than a funk vamp, and `chordToneBias` 0.80 for a re-performance rather than a collage. ⚠ `medium` on the research's high-medium. INFERRED: the ii–V's position in the cycle — the research names the device, not the bar it lands on — and the 4-bar loop weighting.",
